{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a430c6c730ca606890a6d00ef4c","type":"dcr","status":"implementing","title":"Replace UUID element references with generalized XPaths in query_all and page_section","description":"query_all returns element IDs that are internal UUIDs (e.g. `5745d6fd-9ea1-48d0-847d-37db434f6e11`). LLM agents consistently try to use these as CSS selectors (`#5745d6fd-...`), which fails because CSS IDs can't start with digits. This wastes 2-5 tool calls per session and is the #1 source of cobrowser errors in agentic workflows.\n\n## Problem (data-driven)\n- Measured across 148 real elements from Amazon/Best Buy test sessions\n- Status quo selectors: mean 55.8 tokens, 49% reliability\n- Generalized XPaths: mean 10.7 tokens, ~95% reliability\n- 5x token savings, near-double reliability\n\n## Proposed Change\nReplace UUID-based element references with well-generalized XPaths throughout the cobrowser pipeline:\n1. `query_all` response: return `xpath` field instead of/alongside `selector`\n2. `page_section` / `cobrowser_read`: accept `xpath` parameter (use `document.evaluate`)\n3. Add `getSmartXPath(element)` function to the Firefox extension\n\n## XPath Generation Strategy (attribute-priority cascade)\nFor each element, walk up ancestors. At each level try:\n1. Stable `@id` (skip UUID-like: `/^[0-9a-f]{8}-/`)\n2. `@data-testid` / `@aria-label` / `@role`\n3. Semantic `@class` (skip generated: `/^(css-|r-|sg-col|_[A-Z])/`)\n4. `tag[position()]` among same-tag siblings (last resort)\nStop when path uniquely identifies element (verify with `document.evaluate`).\n\nGood: `//div[contains(@class,\"s-result-item\")][3]`\nBad: `/html/body/div[6]/div/main/div/ul/li[3]`\n\n## Future: Hybrid XPath + Custom Refs\nConsider adding opaque `ref:N` handles alongside XPaths for maximum token efficiency (3 tokens vs 10.7). Refs would be session-scoped WeakMap entries resolved server-side. XPath for composability (agents can add predicates), refs for passthrough.\nStart with XPath only. Experiment with hybrid in a second step, data-driven — measure whether refs improve round efficiency vs XPath alone. User intuition: refs may be fragile at runtime (reason unclear — needs investigation before committing).","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:24:32","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:33:01","priority":2,"tags":["firefox-extension","page-section","query-all","reliability","token-efficiency","xpath"]}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b","type":"work_item","status":"in_progress","title":"Implementation plan: Generalized XPath element references","description":"Implementation plan for DCR: Replace UUID element references with generalized XPaths.\n\n## Architecture\nAll changes are in ~/github/HumanWeb. The Firefox extension (JS) generates XPaths since it has the live DOM. The Python service passes them through. MCP tools expose the new parameter.\n\n## Phases\n1. Core: getSmartXPath() function in Firefox extension\n2. Integration: Wire into query_all response + page_section/read acceptance\n3. Validation: Test on Amazon + Best Buy, measure token savings and reliability\n4. Minerva skill update: Update Co-Browser Automation skill to reference xpath parameter","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:11","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:33:01","tags":["implementation","plan","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a430c6c730ca606890a6d00ef4c"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a44b1de773eb3191653f4ab332e","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Implement getSmartXPath() in Firefox extension","description":"Add getSmartXPath(element) function to the Firefox extension JS code.\n\nAlgorithm: attribute-priority cascade, walking up ancestors:\n1. Stable @id (skip UUID-like: /^[0-9a-f]{8}-/)\n2. @data-testid / @aria-label / @role\n3. Semantic @class — blocklist generated patterns: /^(css-|r-|sg-col|_[A-Z]|sc-|styled-|emotion-|chakra-)/\n4. tag[position()] among same-tag siblings (last resort)\n\nStop when path uniquely identifies element (verify with document.evaluate, count=1).\n\nAlso add isGeneratedAttribute(value) heuristic and findSemanticClass(classList) helper.\n\nEstimate: ~100-150 lines of JS.","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:20","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:33:16","tags":["firefox-extension","javascript","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a44be4d7751a5ad6f4c69992260","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Wire XPath into query_all response","description":"Modify the query_all command handler in the Firefox extension to call getSmartXPath() for each matched element and include an `xpath` field in the response.\n\nCurrent response per element: {class, id, index, selector, tagName, text, type, value}\nNew: add `xpath` field.\n\nKeep existing `selector` field for backward compatibility. Agents should prefer `xpath`.","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:23","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:34:02","tags":["firefox-extension","query-all","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a44cca0787b863fc223672b7a29","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Accept xpath parameter in page_section and cobrowser_read","description":"Modify page_section (getSection) and cobrowser_read command handlers to accept an optional `xpath` parameter alongside the existing `selector` parameter.\n\nWhen xpath is provided, use document.evaluate() to locate the element instead of querySelector().\n\nUpdate the MCP tool schemas in mcp_server.py to include the xpath parameter in cobrowser_page_section and cobrowser_read tool definitions.\n\nIf both xpath and selector are provided, prefer xpath.","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:26","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:33:18","tags":["cobrowser-read","mcp","page-section","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a44e2b278efabe46848e5bc716d","type":"work_item","status":"backlog","title":"Validate XPath on Amazon + Best Buy test pages","description":"Test the XPath implementation on real pages:\n\n1. Amazon search results (USB-C cable, sorted price low-to-high)\n2. Best Buy search results (USB-C cable)\n\nFor each page:\n- Run query_all, verify xpath field is present and well-formed\n- Use returned xpaths in page_section calls, verify correct element is returned\n- Measure: tokens per xpath (target: mean <12), resolution success rate (target: >95%)\n- Compare to baseline CSS selectors from prior test sessions\n- Check edge cases: sponsored items, lazy-loaded prices, pagination\n\nUse /tmp/analyze_chat_tokens.py and /tmp/score_selectors.py for measurement.","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:32","updated_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:32","tags":["testing","token-efficiency","validation","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b"}
{"_type":"item","id":"019d6a44f31b7a69bd78de16be215440","type":"work_item","status":"done","title":"Update Co-Browser Automation skill for xpath usage","description":"Update the Co-Browser Automation skill in Minerva's master.dct to guide agents toward using xpath:\n\n- Step 5 (page_section): mention xpath parameter, prefer over selector\n- Step 6 (query_all): note that results include xpath field, use it for subsequent page_section calls\n- Add guidance: 'Use the xpath field from query_all results when calling page_section — do NOT use element IDs as CSS selectors'\n\nThis change goes in ~/github/Minerva/src/Data/master.dct (Co-Browser Automation skill).","created_at":"2026-04-07T23:26:36","updated_at":"2026-04-08T00:53:10","tags":["master-dct","minerva","skill","xpath"],"parent":"cobrowser:019d6a4491e67924be80ef269e49ef6b"}
